WEBVTT

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.810
<i>Hakone Academy third-year 
Ashikiba Takuto narrowly</i>

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:11.110
<i>wins the first day of the Inter-High!</i>

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:16.870
<i>The riders behind him are 
finishing one after another!</i>

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.160
<i>Hakone Academy are striking victory poses!</i>

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.290
<i>His teammates are celebrating 
because they know he's won!</i>

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.170
Hakone Academy! Hakone Academy!

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.640
Naruko-kun...

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.580
Damn it!

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.690
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.770
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:21.160
<b>Inter-High
 Road Race</b>

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.410
<i>More riders are crossing the finish line.</i>

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.510
<i>LINE.06 Sohoku Shaken</i>

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.330
<i>#114, Iwakuni High's Okutani,</i>

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:24.420
<i>and Kyoto Fushimi High's 
Mizuta and Yamaguchi.</i>

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.670
<i>Behind them are Kiriya and Funazu.</i>

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.740
It's time for the award ceremony!

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.590
The winner of the first 
day is Hakone Academy!

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:47.850
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.540
#11, Ashikiba Takuto!

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:47.850
At 202 centimeters tall, the race's tallest 
participant ever has won this honor!

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:50.040
Nice, Hakone Academy!

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.290
The champs are back!

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.210
Congratulations!

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.980
He's huge when he spreads his arms.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.310
Finishing second on the first day are

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.650
Sohoku High School's Naruko Shoukichi and

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.980
Kyoto Fushimi High School's Midousuji Akira!

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.250
Look this way.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.730
Thank you, thank you.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.520
I am Naruko Shoukichi.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.890
He's full of energy!

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.300
Thank you.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.300
I was rooting for you!

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.760
Kyoto Fushimi sent a stand-in.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.430
Is he not feeling well?

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.720
Thank you.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.970
Anyway, Sohoku's way shorter 
than Hakone Academy.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.910
Is Sohoku's rider a bean?

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.780
Hey, you! I can hear you!

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.340
Who are you calling a bean?

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.190
Hey!

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.830
My mic...

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.760
It's the platform!
 It's because of the platform!

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.380
I see.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.770
What are you trying to say, huh? Hey!

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:52.790
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:49.110
Are you making fun of me? Are you?

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.410
Sohoku's #3 is a funny guy!

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.920
You think I'm small, don't you?

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.920
Is this a comedy sketch?

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.550
Give that back!

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:59.750
The first day's winner, Ashikiba, will receive 
a yellow number tag from Miss Nikkou.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:06.800
<b>Miss Nikkou</b>

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:05.240
Tomorrow, he'll get to wear this 
winner's number tag as he rides.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.800
Hakone Academy!

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.600
Next are the other awards.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.100
The winner of the first day's

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:17.700
first result green number tag 
and mark of the fastest sprinter

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.840
is Hakone Academy second-year 
Doubashi Masakiyo!

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.500
Doubashi!

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.290
He's huge, too!

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.210
The winner of the first 
day's red number tag and

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.410
King of the Mountain is Manami Sangaku!

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.560
Manami-kun!

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.170
<b>Manami-kun</b>

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.170
<b>Manami</b>

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.170
Why's he the only one wearing regular shorts?

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.510
The champions have reclaimed their throne!

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.780
The Kanagawa champions Hakone Academy

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:48.970
have won all three of the first day's number tags!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.090
I did it!

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.800
I am Hakone Academy!

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.720
They're incredible.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:54.810
I might become their fan.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.230
<i>Well done, boys.</i>

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:00.440
<i>This is how Hakone Academy should be.</i>

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.610
Abs! We're up!

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.920
We are strong! We are right!

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.690
Thank you for your powerful comments.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.500
That was Doubashi.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.710
Damn, damn, damn! Second!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.610
Second, second, second!

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.930
We placed second in everything!

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.490
Hakone Academy took the 
sprint and the mountains!

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:23.960
How could we place second 
at the finish line, too?

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.280
Who called me a bean?

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.720
So why is Naruko-san cracking jokes?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.370
Doesn't he realize what happened?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.240
Is he stupid?

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.680
Is he not frustrated?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.380
Stop, Issa!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:34.220
No, I'm gonna say it!

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:37.240
Isn't that the reason we placed second?

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.360
That's why Naruko-san lost!

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:41.990
Imaizumi-kun!

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.320
Don't stop me, Onoda.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.610
I'm going to teach this idiot.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.210
What? Idiot?

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.200
Who are you talking about? Me?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:52.370
Naruko sprinted as hard as 
he could for the finish line.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.750
I was right behind him. I know.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.090
They were neck and neck.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:01.840
Midousuji attacked first, 
and Naruko responded.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:07.340
He threw his bike forward so he 
could win precisely and certainly.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.310
His timing wasn't off.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.430
I thought he won.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:19.650
But Hakone Academy's Ashikiba threw 
his bike at the exact same time.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.190
Ashikiba won.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.000
Do you know why?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.990
You think Naruko isn't frustrated?

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.320
No one's more frustrated than him.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:36.600
He lost because of their difference 
in height. Their reach.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.810
Naruko Shoukichi can get laughs, too!

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.470
Don't forget that!

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.460
See you guys tomorrow!

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:47.430
Here.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.850
Knowing he can do nothing about his height,

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:56.980
he's biting back his frustration 
and standing onstage.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:00.980
He's a strong man.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.220
Naruko...

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.010
Man, I'm beat.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:17.410
People love a funny, strong man.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.580
I was mobbed for autographs and photos.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.010
<b>Award
 Inter-High Road Race Day 1
 Second Place
 Sohoku High School  Naruko Shoukichi-dono</b>

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.450
I can finally relax.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:41.390
There's nobody here.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.310
<b>Award
 Inter-High Road Race Day 1
 Second Place</b>

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.920
Relax... Re...

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:56.200
Damn it!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.330
<b>Chiba Sohoku High School</b>

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.920
Are you all right, Teshima-san?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.040
Junta!

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.370
I'm okay.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:15.880
He doesn't look okay to me!

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.860
He's sweating bullets!

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.030
Yeah.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:21.130
I'll massage your back.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.100
Thanks, Gorizo.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.430
Here's a cold towel.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.530
Thanks.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.610
Where's Naruko?

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.530
Not so hard, Gorizo.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.370
Sorry.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:37.250
Did anyone go to Naruko's award ceremony?

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:43.620
Yes. Sugimoto-kun, Sawada-kun, and the 
other first-years took photos and a video.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.920
They applauded for him, too.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.560
Second overall at the Inter-High.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.210
We made it to the podium.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.590
Make sure you praise him when he comes back.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:54.900
<i>Teshima-san...</i>

00:08:56.330 --> 00:09:00.220
<i>He gave everything he had against 
Manami-kun in the mountain stage.</i>

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.930
<i>He can't ride anymore.</i>

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.760
<i>He pushed himself really hard 
to reach the finish line.</i>

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:17.030
<i>I was supposed to do that work for
our second Inter-High, but I...</i>

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.380
<i>I'm a second-year now.</i>

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.600
<i>No! I can't let my thoughts get dark.</i>

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.510
<i>I know. If anything, I should be cheerful.</i>

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:26.810
<i>I'll cheer everyone up.</i>

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:29.670
<i>As a second-year, I should 
keep everyone's spirits up.</i>

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.470
<i>I know. I'll tell a joke.</i>

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.610
<i>Okay, um...</i>

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:34.340
Onoda...

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:35.880
Who?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.220
Oh, yes?

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:41.720
Thanks for carrying me to the finish line.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.460
Oh, no problem.

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:49.410
But I should've been the one to race 
in the first day's mountain stage.

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:53.610
I'm sorry I got separated from the team.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:58.980
You did well to break through their
 tag #1 barrier and ride to the front.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.060
It must've been hard.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:04.240
Didn't Kyoto try to slow 
you down on your way there?

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:09.030
Compared to you, I hardly did anything.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:10.880
Um...

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:14.840
Thanks to you, all six of us finished.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.670
Yes, sir.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:20.780
Don't they race again tomorrow?

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:21.260
Huh?

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.770
Can Teshima-san race like this?

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:29.190
Huh?

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:41.590
<i>Huh? The ground's getting closer...</i>

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.490
<i>Why is it getting closer?</i>

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:47.850
Issa!

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:48.660
Kaburagi!

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.850
<i>I collapsed?</i>

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.370
<i>That's impossible.</i>

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:57.920
<i>That was only the first day
 of the Inter-High...</i>

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.970
K-K-K-K-Kaburagi-kun!

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.480
Leave him on the ground, Onoda.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:03.930
Did he just lose consciousness?

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.640
Another member?

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.700
Call the first-aid tent.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:08.930
And bring some cold water.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:14.230
<i>He was angrily ranting about 
Naruko until a second ago!</i>

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:19.490
<i>Your adrenaline keeps you energized 
during and after a race.</i>

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.600
Bring him inside.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:17.750
Get three towels.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:18.530
Yes, sir.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:27.010
<i>But once that runs out, all the exhaustion 
that's built up hits you at once.</i>

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:30.500
<i>I should've forced him to cool down.</i>

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:33.380
<i>I had my hands full with myself.</i>

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:37.270
<i>I can't believe the team is this damaged.</i>

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.380
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.300
Ice water.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:39.910
Got it.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:45.210
<i>You're an important part of 
this team, too, Kaburagi Issa.</i>

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:47.260
Onoda...

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:48.600
Yes?

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:50.810
Go look for Naruko.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:59.860
There's something we all need to talk 
about before we head to the hotel.

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:03.300
<i>Where is Naruko-kun?</i>

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:05.540
<i>The awards ceremony is over.</i>

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:06.580
Ouch...

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.330
My legs are sore.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:12.100
<i>I wonder what he wants to talk about.</i>

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:13.870
<i>Is it important?</i>

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.670
Kaburagi and I can't race tomorrow.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.970
The four of you have to race.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.590
Good luck.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:25.010
No, no! Makishima-san said 
bad thoughts bring bad results.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.710
<i>The six of us will ride.</i>

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.890
I'm sure we'll be fine.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:38.090
Sohoku is a team that supports each other!

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:40.550
Kinjou-san said the same thing last year!

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:41.810
<i>Kinjou-san...</i>

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:50.940
What?

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.490
You sure, Makishima?

00:12:58.490 --> 00:12:59.420
Yeah.

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:02.220
It's your decision to make.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.200
You traveled the farthest.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:06.840
This is fine.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:11.720
Huh?

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:18.360
What?

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:23.450
Kinjou-san?

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:27.410
We were watching at the finish line.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:30.410
You've put together a good team, Onoda.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:32.470
Kinjou-san...

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:34.870
Kinjou-san!

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:36.790
It's been a while.

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:39.620
Looks like you've grown a little.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:41.530
Your face has changed.

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:43.770
Huh? Really?

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:46.210
Y-You came to cheer us on?

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:48.480
Th-Thank you!

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.100
It's really you!

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:56.130
The team's in trouble.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:14:00.440
Teshima-san is exhausted, and our 
first-year Kaburagi-kun collapsed.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:04.690
Come to our tent.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.530
Everyone will be glad to see you.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:09.850
A visit from you will cheer them up.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:10.890
It's this way.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.370
I can't.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.710
Y-You have something to do? You're busy?

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.000
But couldn't you just stop by?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.130
I-Isn't Sohoku a team that supports each other?

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.380
You're the ones who support each other.

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.550
Huh?

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:33.010
You're the only ones within arm's 
reach when you need each other.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:36.770
We've already graduated.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.230
We can't support you anymore.

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:53.910
Onoda, where have you been?

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.510
Naruko came back already.

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.450
Sorry I'm late.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:00.150
Let's get this team meeting 
started, Onoda-kun.

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:00.900
Okay.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:06.370
We gave everything we had. All six of us.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.500
And we lost.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:12.880
Naruko did his best, but in the end,
 he couldn't make it.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.220
It was a close second.

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:20.550
<i>Teshima-san and Kaburagi 
were close seconds, too.</i>

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:23.730
<i>We were beaten at the very last second.</i>

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:27.480
The answer I've drawn from this...

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.620
...is that we're still only challengers!

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:37.290
Hakone Academy is strong.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.510
The fans have high hopes for them, too.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:41.510
And we can't underestimate Kyoto Fushimi.

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:42.960
So...

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.210
There's only one thing for us to do.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:47.500
It's the same as last year.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:52.680
We'll persistently hang on until we're 
exhausted, try and fail repeatedly,

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:56.510
find the tiniest of opportunities,
 and seize them.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:00.920
We'll entrust our souls to each other
 and ride as hard as we can.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:04.410
We'll help and support each 
other and never give up.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:07.160
We just have to ride the way Sohoku rides!

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:09.530
Is that our only option?

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.630
It's an exhausting way to ride.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.160
That's right.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.830
I have an announcement.

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:25.580
I just ran into Kinjou-san 
at the Inter-High grounds.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.500
Kin...

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.220
What?

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.370
Kinjou-san's here?

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:32.980
Captain Shades is here?

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:35.000
Oh, I guess he's not the captain anymore.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.220
And Tadokoro-san and Makishima-san?

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.430
Are they coming by the tent later?

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:41.600
They said they couldn't see us.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:42.890
What?

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:50.070
Wh-Why not? It could be for just a second.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.150
I know it would make everyone happy.

00:16:56.920 --> 00:17:00.390
At first, we planned to visit 
your tent and praise you guys.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:06.610
But on the first day, Sohoku just 
barely let their chance slip away.

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:07.830
We thought it would be dangerous.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.640
All the more reason for you to come.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.070
The power to avoid a dangerous situation

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:20.970
or turn that into a victory only lies 
within the individual or the team.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:24.480
<i>Kinjou-san was actually...</i>

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:28.390
If we go, the tension will be shattered.

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:30.170
You'll lose sight of what you have to do.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:31.970
It'll divide the team.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:37.610
You're at your weakest right now.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.620
That's why we can't go.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.850
You must understand that, Onoda.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:46.980
<i>He was thinking of us.</i>

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:52.980
Struggle against your difficult 
circumstances, Onoda.

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.510
That will surely give rise to something.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:56.970
Yes, sir.

00:17:58.310 --> 00:17:59.250
Good.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.720
<i>You have the face of a 
second-year now, Onoda.</i>

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:08.230
We were going to leave without seeing anyone,
 but I'm glad I got to talk to you.

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:11.580
The three of us decided we 
wouldn't see anyone today.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:12.710
The three of you?

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.210
I know it's hard, but try to understand.

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:19.860
But we plan to stick around and watch 
the race for as long as we can.

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:25.580
Go back and tell the others 
that we'll be watching.

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:30.170
Um... three of you?

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:36.390
Yeah. Makishima came, too.

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:38.420
All the way from England.

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:45.350
<i>M-Makishima-san is at the race?</i>

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:47.850
<i>He's in Japan?</i>

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.860
M-Makishima-san...

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.740
<i>Does it hurt not to see him, Onoda?</i>

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:56.860
<i>I'm sure it does.</i>

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:01.450
Dear Brother

00:18:57.430 --> 00:19:00.440
<i>Makishima said he's gotten a 
lot of letters from you.</i>

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:04.170
<i>But it's Makishima's decision.</i>

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:07.570
Does it hurt, Onoda?

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:15.640
Makishima-san is here.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:20.630
He's watching us race.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.450
I'm glad!

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.140
So they can't come see us.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.930
He's tough.

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:34.770
What is he, a rock?

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:36.770
Tadokoro-san...

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.750
So that's how it is.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.700
They can't support us when we're weak.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.270
So...

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.410
Let's get stronger.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.870
We'll become stronger.

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:53.210
<i>This rising pressure...</i>

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:57.880
<i>Kinjou-san described 
Onoda that way last year.</i>

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:03.050
Let's show them our new Sohoku!

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.310
<i>Those forward-facing eyes...</i>

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:07.970
<i>This is what moved Sohoku last year.</i>

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:12.020
That's it. It's simple, 
but you're right, Onoda.

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:13.970
Of course.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.480
In that case, let's shock them.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:18.360
So they won't see us until we win?

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:20.990
His orders are as difficult as ever.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.410
We have to be number one.

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:31.200
Let's do it again tomorrow, Sohoku!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.960
Yeah!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.130
All right!

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:40.230
Oh.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.430
We forgot someone.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.680
What?

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:00.230
"I'm glad," huh?

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:04.200
Onoda's still a surprising guy.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:07.300
Sounds like Onoda.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:13.270
By the way, where are we staying tonight?

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:17.450
It's a little cramped,
 but we can stay at my place.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.090
We're going back?

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:53.930
<b><i>Bicycle Country
 Cycle Sports Center
 Cycling Hot Springs  Yu Salon</i></b>

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:00.890
Don't do it, Naruko-kun!

00:23:00.890 --> 00:23:02.900
Don't try to stop me, Onoda-kun!

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:03.720
This itch...

00:23:03.720 --> 00:23:06.570
I have to push him!

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:10.990
Naruko, he'll kill you later!

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:12.870
Hey, wait!

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:17.170
Stop, Naruko-kun!

00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:18.250
Don't stop me!

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.370
No!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:36.130
What are you doing?

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT RIDE Footsteps of Hope</i>

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:44.900
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:51.500
<b>Mura</b>
